We are opening a call for expressions of interest in the post of an ICT Systems Specialist. The Directorate-General for Digitalisation, Information Technology and Cybersecurity (DITEC) is looking for a motivated ICT Systems Specialist to join the Central Infrastructure Sector (OPC). The successful candidate will work closely with colleagues across the General Secretariat of the Council (GSC) to deploy, monitor, support and troubleshoot the storage and back-up infrastructures. The role covers a wide range of activities, including providing level 3 support, managing the daily data back-ups and restores, maintaining and improving the back-up infrastructure and managing the storage offering (block/SAN, file/NAS and object storage solutions). If you think you would like to contribute to shaping secure and innovative digital services, we would love to hear from you!

We are

In partnership with delegates and staff, the Directorate-General for Digitalisation, Information Technology and Cybersecurity (DITEC), organises information and makes it accessible through smart and secure services. We help transform work by innovating and promoting a "digital-first" mindset. Our team is composed of dynamic and motivated colleagues, committed to developing digital services to transform and improve the way the General Secretariat of the Council (GSC) works. The Directorate-General comprises three directorates: Directorate 1 – Digitalisation; Directorate 2 – Communication and Information Systems and Directorate 3 – Cybersecurity.

The ”Infrastructure and Operations” (RUN) Unit is part of the Communication and Information Systems Directorate. It delivers high-quality secure communication and information services by operating communication and information systems and maintaining their infrastructure in line with best practices and in the most cost-effective way. We work closely with clients across the GSC to deliver user-friendly IT tools and sound information management policies. Our applications add value to and facilitate the GSC’s activities.

The Central Infrastructure (CI) sector of the Infrastructure and Operations (RUN) unit of the GSC’s Communication and Information Systems Directorate is responsible for the implementation and operational management of the computing and storage infrastructures. The sector’s mission is, among other things, to provide support for the GSC’s applications. Core services that are provided include computing and storage services.

The General Secretariat of the Council (GSC) is the body responsible for assisting two European Union (EU) institutions: the European Council and the Council of the EU, including their presidencies, the Permanent Representatives Committee (Coreper) and the other Council committees and working parties.

The GSC organises and ensures the coherence of the Council’s work and the implementation of its 18-month programme. In summary, the GSC plays a vital role in ensuring effective functioning and coordination within the EU's decision-making bodies.

We offer

Reporting to the Head of Office, you will take care of the continuous improvement and fine-tuning of the storage and back-up infrastructure. You will ensure the proper functioning of daily IT operations in a pro-active and re-active (incident-solving) way.

You will use and develop your excellent technical knowledge and communication skills to propose new measures/technical solutions to improve the Central Infrastructure service.

Working in a very dynamic environment, you will provide administrative and technical assistance to senior management in the field of Communication and Information Systems (CIS) in order to make systems, tools and services available. You will have the opportunity to manage, operate and use storage and back-up equipment and tools in the area of communication and information systems (CIS) to maximise the availability of systems, applications and services.

You will be expected to efficiently support the continuous operations of our systems and services, to carry out general tasks such as implementing decisions and monitoring the implementation of activity programmes.

Through your involvement in drafting and/or implementing policies and strategies, and in conducting studies and evaluations, in particular relating to technology watching, you will contribute to the success of our IT services.

In this role, you will liaise with many internal and external contacts.

